<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73862" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμό-τῑμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ʽτιμἤ</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>equally valued</i> or
				<i>honoured, held in equal honour,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				15.186
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μακάρεσσι</span>
			<i>with</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				17.16
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μακάρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					7.103
				</span></i>
			 : c. gen. rei, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς στρατηγίας ὁ.</span>
			<i>having an equal share in</i> the command, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Fab.</u>
				9
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ "τῶν ὁμοτίμων"
			καλούμενοι,</span> among the Persians, <i>chief nobles, peers,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				2.1.9
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				7.5.85
			</span></i> : as title at the court of the Ptolemies, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ὁ. τοῖς συγγενέσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PTeb.</u>
					254
				</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PPar.</u>
				15.20
			</span></i><span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristaenet.
					1.3
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Phlp.
				<u>in APr.</u>
				13.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>in AP</u>
				0.367.9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>equal in degree,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σηπεδὼν ἐν ἅπασι τοῖς ἀγγείοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					10.745
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.653
				</span></i>
			, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. οἱ χυμοὶ διασήπονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					10.606
				</span></i>
			, cf.<i><span class="en">
				Ascl.
				<u>in Metaph.</u>
				226.32
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Steph.
				<u>in Gal.</u>
				1.270
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>: c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς ἰδίοις . . γνωρίσμασι τὰ
					συνακολουθοῦντα πολλάκις ὁ. γράφων</span>”
				<i>no less than . . , </i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					9.385
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
